      "sourceFacts": [
        "Two separate manufactured packages, vertically separated in the original, with no circuit connection between them.",
        "Upper package: upright rounded rectangular metal case with a perspective lid, visible front and left side, lid/body seams and two bottom mounting feet; the left foot has a visible mounting opening.",
        "Exactly two bent upright top terminals with individual eyes/holes and separate dark insulating bases. No conductor joins the two lugs.",
        "Front panel has manufacturer/type/rating-like print and a small emblem. The scan does not support reliable transcription of these characters or numeric ratings.",
        "Lower package: short cylinder tilted upward to the right, left circular end, sleeve and right rim, with a marking region.",
        "One axial lead leaves each opposite end of the smaller package: down-left and up-right. Neither lead joins the upper package.",
        "No visible interior winding, layer section, polarity, numerical exercise given, grid, axis or measurement is supplied by these source pixels."
      ],
      "modernAdditionsNotSourceFacts": [
        "Plain English identification and neutral marking regions replace unreadable historical lettering and emblem without fabricated ratings.",
        "Repositioning the small package to the right preserves the identity and independence of both source examples.",
        "The enlarged spiral roll and two alternating foil/paper strips are edition-derived instructional additions, not a source cutaway. Their size and turn count are schematic."
      ],
